<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 90-day T-bill yields avg 2.799 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 90-day T-bill yields avg 2.799 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 90-day Government of Canada treasury bills due April 3, 1997 was 2.799 percent, down from 2.875 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 181-day T-bills due July 3, 1997 was 3.176 percent, down from 3.257 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 354-day T-bills due December 23, 1997 was 3.541 percent, down from 3.607 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$500 billion three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$150 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.0 billion of C$6.9 billion of bills due Jan 9. (Details follow)  </p>
